1
00:00:33,916 --> 00:00:34,916
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:34,916 --> 00:00:35,916
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:35,916 --> 00:00:37,483
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:41,283 --> 00:00:47,168
[Winter, 2011]

5
00:00:47,168 --> 00:00:51,740
Come on, I told you to order something
expensive. Get some boiled pork too.

6
00:00:51,740 --> 00:00:53,324
You're a college student.
How much money could you have?

7
00:00:53,324 --> 00:00:55,312
It's fine. This is enough.

8
00:00:55,312 --> 00:00:57,584
I work part-time.

9
00:00:57,584 --> 00:00:59,152
I have more money than you.

10
00:00:59,152 --> 00:01:01,360
How? You're just
a civil service exam student.

11
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:03,083
My mom.

12
00:01:03,836 --> 00:01:06,183
She's been saving up more than I realized.

13
00:01:09,348 --> 00:01:11,476
Is studying for the police exam going okay?

14
00:01:11,476 --> 00:01:12,840
I guess it's just right for me.

15
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:14,212
It really sticks in my head.

16
00:01:14,212 --> 00:01:15,636
Just wait and see.

17
00:01:15,636 --> 00:01:20,468
I'll be wearing a badge within two years,
and I'll catch that punk myself.

18
00:01:20,468 --> 00:01:22,460
And then what, after you catch him?

19
00:01:22,460 --> 00:01:24,008
After that?

20
00:01:24,008 --> 00:01:25,276
Then I'll catch the next punk.

21
00:01:25,276 --> 00:01:27,016
Jeez, forget it, you punk.

22
00:01:27,648 --> 00:01:30,649
You talked me into being a reporter,
and now you're betraying me.

23
00:01:30,649 --> 00:01:32,049
The more I think about it,
the more pissed off I get.

24
00:01:32,049 --> 00:01:35,584
Hey, if we're all digging,
who's going to catch the fish?

25
00:01:35,584 --> 00:01:37,268
You just keep digging.

26
00:01:37,268 --> 00:01:39,024
I'll catch the fish.

27
00:01:39,024 --> 00:01:41,504
You do your job, and I'll do mine.

28
00:01:41,504 --> 00:01:43,036
Bang, bang!

29
00:01:43,036 --> 00:01:44,144
Oh, please.

30
00:01:44,144 --> 00:01:46,604
Don't get beaten to a pulp
by some criminal later.

31
00:01:46,604 --> 00:01:49,588
- Ma'am, could you turn up the TV?
- Sure.

32
00:01:49,588 --> 00:01:52,069
[Police Focused on Kingfisher Investigation]
<i>The shooting incidents</i>

33
00:01:52,069 --> 00:01:56,000
<i>by the serial killer known as Kingfisher
have risen to nine.</i>

34
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,420
<i>Police have concluded that
last week's shooting in Cheongsin-dong</i>

35
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:01,456
[Kingfisher Shootings Rise to 9]
<i>was also the work of the same suspect.</i>

36
00:02:01,456 --> 00:02:04,283
[Cheongsin-dong Case Also Same Culprit]
<i>They are intensifying their investigation.</i>

37
00:02:04,283 --> 00:02:08,308
<i>Meanwhile, the number of members
in an online Kingfisher fan club</i>

38
00:02:08,308 --> 00:02:09,936
- <i>is approaching 300,000...</i>
- A fan club?

39
00:02:09,936 --> 00:02:11,583
Have they all lost their darn minds?

40
00:02:11,583 --> 00:02:13,483
Why are they cheering for that lunatic?

41
00:02:13,483 --> 00:02:15,920
Maybe they get
some kind of catharsis from it.

42
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:18,549
He picks out the worst criminals
and kills them.

43
00:02:18,549 --> 00:02:19,616
Catharsis, my foot.

44
00:02:19,616 --> 00:02:23,972
Hey, isn't killing a murderer still murder?

45
00:02:23,972 --> 00:02:26,220
Even if he only kills criminals for now,

46
00:02:26,220 --> 00:02:28,683
who's to say he won't kill
an innocent person someday?

47
00:02:29,577 --> 00:02:33,549
If, by chance, I mean, seriously, what if...

48
00:02:35,408 --> 00:02:38,148
just hypothetically,
Kingfisher killed that punk...

49
00:02:38,148 --> 00:02:40,083
That punk? Who...

50
00:02:42,449 --> 00:02:45,732
Do you really think
I'd feel happy or thankful?

51
00:02:45,732 --> 00:02:48,416
I mean, he'd be taking revenge
for you, or something like that.

52
00:02:48,416 --> 00:02:50,476
Darn it. Hey!

53
00:02:50,476 --> 00:02:54,144
If another murderer kills
my parents' murderer, is that revenge?

54
00:02:54,144 --> 00:02:55,948
If anyone's going to take revenge,
it should be me.

55
00:02:55,948 --> 00:02:58,116
What right does Kingfisher have?

56
00:03:03,996 --> 00:03:06,283
My revenge is

57
00:03:06,283 --> 00:03:10,016
to catch him and put him
in prison for the rest of his life.

58
00:03:10,016 --> 00:03:12,976
To me, they're both the same murdering punk.

59
00:03:12,976 --> 00:03:15,508
Once I catch that punk,

60
00:03:15,508 --> 00:03:19,849
I'll catch Kingfisher next, no matter what.

61
00:03:20,752 --> 00:03:23,000
Just wait and see.

62
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,700
Alright.

63
00:03:29,049 --> 00:03:30,176
Oh, my.

64
00:03:30,176 --> 00:03:33,072
Oh, my, I'm so sorry.

65
00:03:33,072 --> 00:03:36,256
Ma'am, one plate of boiled pork, please.

66
00:03:36,256 --> 00:03:37,676
To cover the dry cleaning.

67
00:03:37,676 --> 00:03:40,383
Keep your strength up, future detective.

68
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,516
Thirty thousand won,
including the boiled pork? Alright.

69
00:03:44,516 --> 00:03:46,216
What's with her?

70
00:03:53,083 --> 00:03:56,116
[Episode 10]

71
00:03:56,116 --> 00:03:58,116
[Client Suitability Assessment,
One-Month Post-Release Observation]

72
00:03:58,116 --> 00:04:00,246
[Multiple Risk Indicators,
High Reoffending Risk]

73
00:04:08,268 --> 00:04:11,449
Why? Because of the victim's son who's a cop?

74
00:04:16,204 --> 00:04:19,876
I thought he looked familiar. Now I remember.

75
00:04:19,876 --> 00:04:25,076
I saw him in the first-floor lobby
when we were leaving your housewarming party.

76
00:04:25,076 --> 00:04:27,252
I've heard about it.

77
00:04:27,252 --> 00:04:29,028
He's a friend of my husband's.

78
00:04:29,028 --> 00:04:30,312
Yeah?

79
00:04:30,312 --> 00:04:32,012
Your husband...

80
00:04:33,036 --> 00:04:35,383
had a friend like that?

81
00:04:36,076 --> 00:04:41,183
If you're really uncomfortable with it,
let's change the scenario.

82
00:04:47,383 --> 00:04:50,232
Why do people never really change?

83
00:04:50,232 --> 00:04:52,900
Twenty years is a pretty long time.

84
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:54,600
Exactly.

85
00:04:55,568 --> 00:04:57,716
They commit sins
that even repentance and remorse

86
00:04:57,716 --> 00:05:00,696
can never make the victims' families forgive.

87
00:05:00,696 --> 00:05:02,348
Why do they even do it?

88
00:05:02,348 --> 00:05:04,083
At times like this,

89
00:05:04,716 --> 00:05:10,216
that saying, "A leopard can't change
its spots," feels so cruel, doesn't it?

90
00:05:10,216 --> 00:05:14,452
But still, not everyone kills just because

91
00:05:14,452 --> 00:05:16,783
they grew up in different
conditions and environments.

92
00:05:16,783 --> 00:05:23,259
Plenty of people serve the time they deserve
and then go on to live new lives.

93
00:05:24,016 --> 00:05:28,183
That's why the law and the state
give them another chance.

94
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:33,983
Let's stick to the scenario.

95
00:05:34,680 --> 00:05:36,383
Will you be okay?

96
00:05:37,066 --> 00:05:38,066
I have to be.

97
00:05:38,066 --> 00:05:42,249
It's my job, and it's what I can do.

98
00:05:55,192 --> 00:05:56,883
<i>Why are you going after that punk, you idiot?</i>

99
00:05:56,883 --> 00:05:59,816
What are you planning to do if you meet him?

100
00:06:00,564 --> 00:06:03,532
What do you mean? I'm just watching him.

101
00:06:03,532 --> 00:06:05,180
Why? What...

102
00:06:05,180 --> 00:06:07,216
Worried the cop might do something reckless?

103
00:06:07,216 --> 00:06:08,868
Especially since I have a gun?

104
00:06:08,868 --> 00:06:11,796
Jeez, even your jokes are messed up.

105
00:06:11,796 --> 00:06:14,088
- Why do you have a gun...
- <i>If you know I'm joking,</i>

106
00:06:14,088 --> 00:06:16,728
stop worrying and go home.

107
00:06:16,728 --> 00:06:18,508
Didn't you say
your wife's working late tonight?

108
00:06:18,508 --> 00:06:20,208
<i>I'm hanging up.</i>

109
00:06:41,583 --> 00:06:42,780
[My Santa]

110
00:06:42,780 --> 00:06:44,444
<i>I'm working late.</i>

111
00:06:44,444 --> 00:06:45,976
<i>Where are you, Tae Seong?</i>

112
00:06:45,976 --> 00:06:47,449
<i>I'm leaving work now.</i>

113
00:06:47,449 --> 00:06:51,112
<i>Se Ah said she'd watch Yul until eight.
I'll make sure I get home before then.</i>

114
00:06:51,112 --> 00:06:53,280
<i>I won't be too late either.</i>

115
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:54,483
<i>I'll call you when I'm done.</i>

116
00:06:54,483 --> 00:06:57,240
[Wednesday, May 6]

117
00:06:57,240 --> 00:06:59,748
<i>Jang Eun Hak is leaving work.</i>

118
00:06:59,748 --> 00:07:02,132
He's expected to arrive in
about five minutes.

119
00:07:02,132 --> 00:07:03,832
<i>Okay.</i>

120
00:07:09,849 --> 00:07:12,116
He's entering the next block.

121
00:07:22,168 --> 00:07:25,683
Looks like he's buying something.
He just went into a convenience store.

122
00:07:26,828 --> 00:07:28,516
<i>Oh...</i>

123
00:07:28,516 --> 00:07:30,400
It's liquor.

124
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:34,856
He grabbed a few bottles of soju
and sat down outside the store.

125
00:07:34,856 --> 00:07:36,783
<i>This could take a while.</i>

126
00:07:45,568 --> 00:07:50,184
Ms. Yoo, there's a man tailing Jang Eun Hak.

127
00:07:50,184 --> 00:07:51,875
- A man?
- <i>Looks like he's been following him</i>

128
00:07:51,875 --> 00:07:52,997
<i>since the workshop.</i>

129
00:07:52,997 --> 00:07:55,668
He's watching him from a distance.

130
00:07:55,668 --> 00:07:57,208
What does he look like?

131
00:07:57,208 --> 00:08:00,196
Wearing a jacket, mid-thirties, maybe?

132
00:08:00,196 --> 00:08:03,728
I can't make out his face on camera.

133
00:08:03,728 --> 00:08:05,449
Let me take a look.

134
00:08:28,432 --> 00:08:31,328
Could it be the son who's a cop...

135
00:08:31,328 --> 00:08:32,936
Yeah, that's him.

136
00:08:32,936 --> 00:08:34,749
Then I guess today...

137
00:08:35,988 --> 00:08:37,916
Let's just watch for now.

138
00:08:51,716 --> 00:08:53,616
Jang Eun Hak is moving.

139
00:08:54,536 --> 00:08:57,192
He's heading back the way he came?

140
00:08:57,192 --> 00:08:58,892
I see him.

141
00:09:16,752 --> 00:09:19,149
Jang Eun Hak has gone back into the workshop.

142
00:09:26,956 --> 00:09:30,352
Ms. Yoo, Jang Eun Hak made a move again.

143
00:09:30,352 --> 00:09:32,883
What? What about the son?

144
00:09:34,044 --> 00:09:35,744
What? Is he hurt?

145
00:09:37,676 --> 00:09:40,012
<i>Jang Eun Hak bolted out.</i>

146
00:09:40,012 --> 00:09:42,616
<i>The son chased right after him.</i>

147
00:09:42,616 --> 00:09:44,749
[Dongwoon Furniture]
He's holding a gun.

148
00:10:02,456 --> 00:10:03,532
I'm heading out.

149
00:10:03,532 --> 00:10:05,416
<i>Track their route and keep me posted.</i>

150
00:10:05,416 --> 00:10:09,376
Ms. Yoo, Kwon Tae Seong is here.

151
00:10:09,376 --> 00:10:10,780
- What?
- <i>He went into the workshop,</i>

152
00:10:10,780 --> 00:10:14,483
came back out, and ran off
in the direction the two of them went.

153
00:10:14,483 --> 00:10:16,368
Why is your husband here...

154
00:10:16,368 --> 00:10:19,152
Ms. Yoo! Ms. Yoo, are you listening?

155
00:10:19,152 --> 00:10:20,544
Yeah, I'm listening.

156
00:10:20,544 --> 00:10:22,492
- Then let's pull out for today...
- No.

157
00:10:22,492 --> 00:10:23,852
<i>If we leave now, we'll lose him.</i>

158
00:10:23,852 --> 00:10:25,552
Keep going.

159
00:10:28,888 --> 00:10:30,388
I'm down. Which way?

160
00:10:30,388 --> 00:10:32,183
<i>Ms. Yoo, what are you going to do?</i>

161
00:10:32,183 --> 00:10:33,576
What if something happens today...

162
00:10:33,576 --> 00:10:35,276
<i>Ki Yeong Do.</i>

163
00:10:39,883 --> 00:10:41,683
With your back to the workshop,
you are on the left.

164
00:10:41,683 --> 00:10:44,656
<i>It's to your right, Ms. Yoo.</i>

165
00:10:44,656 --> 00:10:46,983
Don't take any unnecessary risks.

166
00:11:39,024 --> 00:11:41,049
Jang Eun Hak, stop!

167
00:12:00,876 --> 00:12:02,716
Jang Eun Hak, stop!

168
00:12:19,888 --> 00:12:21,588
Meeting concluded.

169
00:12:23,328 --> 00:12:25,676
Good work, Ms. Yoo.

170
00:12:25,676 --> 00:12:28,360
You should get out of there for now.

171
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:30,060
Dong Jin!

172
00:12:39,592 --> 00:12:40,649
What's wrong with you?

173
00:12:40,649 --> 00:12:42,349
Are you okay?

174
00:12:43,552 --> 00:12:45,252
No...

175
00:12:45,972 --> 00:12:48,052
Not me. I didn't shoot him.

176
00:12:48,052 --> 00:12:52,152
- I know, I know.
- Not me... I...

177
00:12:56,388 --> 00:12:58,088
Kingfisher...

178
00:13:00,592 --> 00:13:02,500
Kingfisher was here.

179
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:04,064
Kingfisher was here... Kingfisher...

180
00:13:04,064 --> 00:13:05,992
Kingfisher... Kingfisher...

181
00:13:05,992 --> 00:13:07,976
Kingfisher...

182
00:13:07,976 --> 00:13:10,683
Dong Jin!

183
00:13:11,449 --> 00:13:12,449
Dong Jin!

184
00:13:12,449 --> 00:13:14,183
No.

185
00:13:14,816 --> 00:13:16,183
You need to get to a hospital first.

186
00:13:16,183 --> 00:13:17,883
You're hurt right now.

187
00:13:17,883 --> 00:13:19,616
I have to catch him.
I have to catch Kingfisher.

188
00:13:19,616 --> 00:13:22,324
You're bleeding badly now!

189
00:13:22,324 --> 00:13:23,532
He was here.

190
00:13:23,532 --> 00:13:26,049
Kingfisher was right here moments ago.

191
00:13:26,049 --> 00:13:28,849
Lee Dong Jin, Lee Dong Jin.

192
00:13:29,472 --> 00:13:30,800
Pull yourself together.

193
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:32,549
You have to stay conscious.

194
00:13:34,684 --> 00:13:36,384
Tae Seong.

195
00:13:39,508 --> 00:13:41,649
That punk, Jang Eun Hak...

196
00:13:44,804 --> 00:13:46,504
is dead.

197
00:13:47,540 --> 00:13:49,316
That punk...

198
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:54,816
He is dead, that punk...

199
00:13:54,816 --> 00:13:58,983
Tae Seong, what do I do? I'm...

200
00:14:01,644 --> 00:14:03,983
I'm so glad that...

201
00:14:07,212 --> 00:14:09,083
Jang Eun Hak is dead.

202
00:14:09,788 --> 00:14:11,488
And...

203
00:14:13,084 --> 00:14:15,452
I'm ashamed of myself for feeling that way.

204
00:14:15,452 --> 00:14:16,804
Dong Jin, it's alright.

205
00:14:16,804 --> 00:14:20,049
Dong Jin, it's alright. It's alright.

206
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:27,116
I was the person in the world
who wanted Jang Eun Hak dead the most.

207
00:14:28,396 --> 00:14:34,040
Every single day, without fail,
I wanted to kill him.

208
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:37,483
Even after twenty years,
whenever I think about that day...

209
00:14:46,384 --> 00:14:49,849
I imagined shooting him over and over again.

210
00:14:50,548 --> 00:14:54,949
I imagined a hole blown through his head,
his entire body torn to shreds,

211
00:14:56,420 --> 00:15:00,475
writhing in agony, then falling into hell.

212
00:15:00,475 --> 00:15:03,050
I wanted desperately to see it
with my own eyes.

213
00:15:03,050 --> 00:15:04,940
I know. I know, Dong Jin.

214
00:15:04,940 --> 00:15:08,032
But first, let's go to the hospital. Please.

215
00:15:08,032 --> 00:15:10,083
Dong Jin, Dong Jin.

216
00:15:10,083 --> 00:15:12,056
You need to go to the hospital first.

217
00:15:12,056 --> 00:15:14,083
I have to catch Kingfisher.

218
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:17,552
He killed that punk!

219
00:15:17,552 --> 00:15:19,949
Kingfisher killed that punk.

220
00:15:19,949 --> 00:15:22,481
For twenty years you pictured it
over and over, but couldn't do it.

221
00:15:22,481 --> 00:15:24,516
Kingfisher did.

222
00:15:24,516 --> 00:15:25,983
You saw it, right?

223
00:15:25,983 --> 00:15:29,656
That punk was trying to kill someone again.

224
00:15:29,656 --> 00:15:32,456
That's right. I couldn't do it.

225
00:15:32,456 --> 00:15:34,948
Even when Jang Eun Hak
was running right in front of me,

226
00:15:34,948 --> 00:15:38,283
with the back of his head
right there in front of me,

227
00:15:39,249 --> 00:15:41,016
I still couldn't kill him.

228
00:15:41,016 --> 00:15:42,749
Do you know why?

229
00:15:44,992 --> 00:15:46,064
You asked me before.

230
00:15:46,064 --> 00:15:48,476
What if he didn't change?

231
00:15:48,476 --> 00:15:50,604
But I already had my answer.

232
00:15:50,604 --> 00:15:53,532
If he commits a crime,
I'll catch him and throw him in.

233
00:15:53,532 --> 00:15:55,896
If he gets out and commits another crime,
I'll catch him and throw him in again.

234
00:15:55,896 --> 00:15:57,316
I'll keep catching him and locking him up.

235
00:15:57,316 --> 00:15:59,932
That's my way,
and it's the right thing to do.

236
00:15:59,932 --> 00:16:04,464
No, in reality, those punks never get judged.

237
00:16:04,464 --> 00:16:08,949
Dong Jin, the law isn't perfect.
And you know that, right?

238
00:16:08,949 --> 00:16:10,449
Oh, yeah?

239
00:16:10,449 --> 00:16:12,649
Then do whatever you want.

240
00:16:12,649 --> 00:16:15,188
I don't care whether the law
is perfect or not.

241
00:16:15,188 --> 00:16:17,528
To me, they're just the same punks
who killed people.

242
00:16:17,528 --> 00:16:19,916
And catching punks like that is my job.

243
00:16:21,980 --> 00:16:24,996
I'll do my job, so you do yours.

244
00:16:24,996 --> 00:16:27,616
Write a story, cover a case, whatever.

245
00:16:27,616 --> 00:16:29,449
You're a reporter, right?

246
00:16:36,980 --> 00:16:39,383
Beom, where are you?

247
00:16:51,484 --> 00:16:52,676
Beom.

248
00:16:52,676 --> 00:16:55,620
Comb through all the nearby CCTV footage
and track his escape route.

249
00:16:55,620 --> 00:16:59,416
And collect every fingerprint, footprint,
and trace evidence around the rooftop.

250
00:16:59,416 --> 00:17:01,216
Okay.

251
00:17:16,024 --> 00:17:17,660
Se Ah.

252
00:17:17,660 --> 00:17:19,688
- Huh? Oh.
- Sorry for waking you.

253
00:17:19,688 --> 00:17:21,052
Bo Na, you're home?

254
00:17:21,052 --> 00:17:24,468
Well, Tae Seong called earlier
saying he'd be late,

255
00:17:24,468 --> 00:17:26,849
so I washed Yul and put her to bed
in the master bedroom.

256
00:17:26,849 --> 00:17:28,925
Sorry I'm late. Thank you.

257
00:17:28,925 --> 00:17:30,716
Go ahead and do what you need to do.

258
00:17:37,800 --> 00:17:38,811
[My Santa]
<i>Something came up.</i>

259
00:17:38,811 --> 00:17:42,716
<i>I'll be really late tonight.
Don't wait up. Go to bed first.</i>

260
00:18:05,649 --> 00:18:07,812
[Did Kingfisher...]

261
00:18:07,812 --> 00:18:09,583
<i>Did Kingfisher...</i>

262
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:12,416
<i>see me too?</i>

263
00:18:25,984 --> 00:18:28,516
<i>That man that day...</i>

264
00:18:29,376 --> 00:18:31,996
<i>Was he really Kingfisher?</i>

265
00:18:31,996 --> 00:18:34,549
<i>Goodnight, Tae Seong.</i>

266
00:18:40,052 --> 00:18:41,960
<i>Tae Seong.</i>

267
00:18:41,960 --> 00:18:45,748
I'll do my job, so you do yours.

268
00:18:45,748 --> 00:18:47,549
<i>You're a reporter, right?</i>

269
00:18:49,183 --> 00:18:50,353
[Did Kingfisher see me too?]

270
00:18:50,353 --> 00:18:52,316
[That man that day...
Was he really Kingfisher?]

271
00:18:57,692 --> 00:19:00,684
<i>Exclusive: Kingfisher Crime Scene.</i>

272
00:19:00,684 --> 00:19:02,816
<i>A supermarket murder convict died</i>

273
00:19:02,816 --> 00:19:06,296
<i>after being shot while fleeing
an attempted murder.</i>

274
00:19:06,296 --> 00:19:09,291
<i>Jang Eun Hak, previously imprisoned
for the murder of a supermarket couple</i>

275
00:19:09,291 --> 00:19:11,376
<i>in Gangmyeon-dong 20 years ago,</i>

276
00:19:11,376 --> 00:19:15,816
<i>died after attempting another murder
just one month after his release on parole.</i>

277
00:19:17,776 --> 00:19:19,273
[Unusual Alleyway Attack]
<i>Another Kingfisher incident</i>

278
00:19:19,273 --> 00:19:21,080
[Kingfisher Strikes Again Last Night]
<i>occurred last night.</i>

279
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:22,747
<i>The victim this time was Mr. Jang,</i>

280
00:19:22,747 --> 00:19:25,944
<i>who had brutally murdered
a supermarket-owning couple 20 years ago.</i>

281
00:19:25,944 --> 00:19:28,005
[Supermarket Murder Convict Shot Dead]
<i>He was sentenced to 16 years,</i>

282
00:19:28,005 --> 00:19:30,121
[While Fleeing After Attempted Murder]
<i>and died a month after being paroled,</i>

283
00:19:30,121 --> 00:19:31,512
[Supermarket Couple Murder Found Dead]
<i>a year before his full term,</i>

284
00:19:31,512 --> 00:19:32,912
[One Month After Parole]
<i>sending shock through the community.</i>

285
00:19:32,912 --> 00:19:33,912
- <i>Moreover, this incident differs from</i>
- They say Kingfisher

286
00:19:33,912 --> 00:19:34,912
- <i>the previous ones,</i>
- struck again yesterday.

287
00:19:34,912 --> 00:19:35,912
- <i>which mainly occurred</i>
- Really?

288
00:19:35,912 --> 00:19:36,912
- <i>in enclosed, isolated spaces.</i>
- Kingfisher is awesome.

289
00:19:36,912 --> 00:19:39,096
<i>Unlike other Kingfisher cases,</i>

290
00:19:39,096 --> 00:19:42,549
<i>this one occurred in a residential alley,
making it highly unusual.</i>

291
00:19:42,549 --> 00:19:45,483
[Exclusive: Kingfisher Crime Scene]
<i>Shockingly, Mr. Jang was revealed</i>

292
00:19:45,483 --> 00:19:47,849
<i>to have attempted to murder his employer.</i>

293
00:19:47,849 --> 00:19:51,293
<i>Just one month after being paroled,
he had committed another attempted murder,</i>

294
00:19:51,293 --> 00:19:52,696
<i>this time as a flagrant offender.</i>

295
00:19:52,696 --> 00:19:55,804
<i>Furthermore, given the urgent situation
with the suspect on the run,</i>

296
00:19:55,804 --> 00:19:57,816
<i>it is speculated that Kingfisher
may have broken from his usual pattern</i>

297
00:19:57,816 --> 00:20:02,083
<i>and carried out the shooting
in a public place.</i>

298
00:20:03,184 --> 00:20:05,052
Mommy, where is Daddy?

299
00:20:05,052 --> 00:20:07,100
Why isn't Daddy waking up?

300
00:20:07,100 --> 00:20:10,440
Dad? Let Daddy sleep a little longer.

301
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:12,749
Is Daddy a sleepyhead?

302
00:20:14,360 --> 00:20:17,116
Daddy worked late last night, so he's tired.

303
00:20:17,116 --> 00:20:18,748
What work?

304
00:20:18,748 --> 00:20:21,208
Writing articles?

305
00:20:21,208 --> 00:20:23,504
What is an article?

306
00:20:23,504 --> 00:20:27,144
An article is something
that tells people in the world

307
00:20:27,144 --> 00:20:32,884
what happened, why it happened,
and what to do now. That's what it does.

308
00:20:32,884 --> 00:20:34,548
Yul, you finished all of this, right?

309
00:20:34,548 --> 00:20:38,236
Oh? You did? Then let's have this.

310
00:20:38,236 --> 00:20:40,620
You said you want to be tall
like Mommy and Daddy, right?

311
00:20:40,620 --> 00:20:42,649
Then you need to eat this
and grow big and tall.

312
00:20:42,649 --> 00:20:44,516
Here, eat.

313
00:20:45,628 --> 00:20:47,128
Is it good?

314
00:20:47,128 --> 00:20:48,176
It is good!

315
00:20:48,176 --> 00:20:49,876
Yeah?

316
00:20:51,924 --> 00:20:53,116
Daddy!

317
00:20:53,116 --> 00:20:55,340
My little precious! Oh, my!

318
00:20:55,340 --> 00:20:57,560
My treasure!

319
00:20:57,560 --> 00:20:59,368
Did you sleep well?

320
00:20:59,368 --> 00:21:00,683
You're already all dressed?

321
00:21:00,683 --> 00:21:04,383
Yeah. I'm dressed, and I ate this too.

322
00:21:04,383 --> 00:21:07,104
I'm going to be this tall, just like you.

323
00:21:07,104 --> 00:21:08,948
Wow, really? Good job.

324
00:21:08,948 --> 00:21:10,032
Sorry, I overslept.

325
00:21:10,032 --> 00:21:13,856
I will make it up to you tomorrow, okay?

326
00:21:13,856 --> 00:21:16,164
Oh, my.

327
00:21:16,164 --> 00:21:18,268
Why don't you sleep a little longer?
You're already up?

328
00:21:18,268 --> 00:21:20,216
I have to get to work.

329
00:21:24,628 --> 00:21:26,828
You must have been tired
from working late last night too,

330
00:21:26,828 --> 00:21:29,049
and you were probably super busy
all alone today.

331
00:21:34,628 --> 00:21:38,836
What? What's with that meaningful look
so early in the morning...

332
00:21:38,836 --> 00:21:39,836
No, it's not that.

333
00:21:39,836 --> 00:21:42,316
It's the look of someone gazing
at someone precious.

334
00:21:45,180 --> 00:21:48,456
Go wash up. I'll make you some toast.

335
00:21:48,456 --> 00:21:50,272
Just a second.

336
00:21:50,272 --> 00:21:52,616
Let me recharge first.

337
00:21:53,640 --> 00:21:55,340
Me too.

338
00:21:59,292 --> 00:22:01,016
Go wash up.

339
00:22:02,028 --> 00:22:04,516
I'm having two pieces of toast.

340
00:22:06,516 --> 00:22:09,283
[Resignation Letter]

341
00:22:10,684 --> 00:22:12,424
Are you threatening me now?

342
00:22:12,424 --> 00:22:15,096
Say it to my face.
Don't do this with a piece of paper.

343
00:22:15,096 --> 00:22:16,622
I know there's
a Kingfisher countermeasure meeting today,

344
00:22:16,622 --> 00:22:18,796
chaired by the Commissioner General.

345
00:22:18,796 --> 00:22:20,020
So what?

346
00:22:20,020 --> 00:22:21,420
How many times have chiefs had meetings?

347
00:22:21,420 --> 00:22:22,872
Don't you know
those meetings are just for show?

348
00:22:22,872 --> 00:22:24,580
Then please make sure
this one isn't just for show.

349
00:22:24,580 --> 00:22:26,096
How exactly am I supposed to do that?

350
00:22:26,096 --> 00:22:28,456
What, you want me to put you in charge?

351
00:22:28,456 --> 00:22:29,520
Why would I?

352
00:22:29,520 --> 00:22:31,349
This is my case.

353
00:22:32,076 --> 00:22:35,112
What were you doing yesterday,
and now you come here?

354
00:22:35,112 --> 00:22:38,020
You finally came face-to-face
with the man you wanted to catch so badly.

355
00:22:38,020 --> 00:22:39,949
But why didn't you catch him?

356
00:22:40,852 --> 00:22:42,552
Jeez.

357
00:22:43,432 --> 00:22:46,420
Other stations asked me
whether you deliberately let him get away.

358
00:22:46,420 --> 00:22:49,748
They think you were stalling to give the guy

359
00:22:49,748 --> 00:22:52,183
who took your revenge for you time to escape.

360
00:22:53,684 --> 00:22:55,780
If that's the case,

361
00:22:55,780 --> 00:22:58,460
it'll be grounds for an investigation
and disciplinary action.

362
00:22:58,460 --> 00:23:04,710
Including why you were lurking around
Jang Eun Hak at that time.

363
00:23:05,552 --> 00:23:08,149
You don't think this will come up
in today's meeting?

364
00:23:12,144 --> 00:23:15,568
Only you know the truth.

365
00:23:15,568 --> 00:23:16,808
I won't ask you about it.

366
00:23:16,808 --> 00:23:18,683
But you need to let it go too.

367
00:23:19,704 --> 00:23:24,780
If an investigation or disciplinary action
comes up, I'll cover for you.

368
00:23:24,780 --> 00:23:26,480
You can go now.

369
00:23:27,828 --> 00:23:30,500
I won't make excuses.
I'll take responsibility.

370
00:23:30,500 --> 00:23:32,452
If they tell me to accept
the punishment, I will.

371
00:23:32,452 --> 00:23:34,236
If they give me a chance, I'll make it right.

372
00:23:34,236 --> 00:23:36,249
And if neither is possible...

373
00:23:36,249 --> 00:23:38,212
[Resignation Letter]

374
00:23:38,212 --> 00:23:40,428
Please accept my resignation.

375
00:23:40,428 --> 00:23:42,204
Hey, take this back.

376
00:23:42,204 --> 00:23:43,664
Hey, Lee Dong Jin.

377
00:23:43,664 --> 00:23:45,416
Hey, Dong Jin.

378
00:23:46,212 --> 00:23:49,649
Jeez, he's bowing, which he never does.

379
00:23:55,588 --> 00:23:57,672
Oh, Mr. Lee.

380
00:23:57,672 --> 00:24:00,308
As expected, all the CCTV footage
around the area was wiped.

381
00:24:00,308 --> 00:24:02,948
It was a no-parking zone, so there wasn't
anything useful from dashcams either.

382
00:24:02,948 --> 00:24:05,480
There's a public parking lot in the back.

383
00:24:05,480 --> 00:24:06,480
I saw it.

384
00:24:06,480 --> 00:24:07,652
You did?

385
00:24:07,652 --> 00:24:10,476
Most of the people living there
work in the furniture district,

386
00:24:10,476 --> 00:24:13,416
so it's normally deserted at that hour
because everyone goes to bed early.

387
00:24:13,416 --> 00:24:16,349
Jeez, and no word on any witnesses, either.

388
00:24:17,200 --> 00:24:18,552
What about forensics?

389
00:24:18,552 --> 00:24:21,532
Nothing yet. Doesn't look like
they recovered much from the scene.

390
00:24:21,532 --> 00:24:24,200
But you never know what might turn up,
so keep checking regularly.

391
00:24:24,200 --> 00:24:25,732
Okay.

392
00:24:25,732 --> 00:24:27,640
But are you okay, Mr. Lee?

393
00:24:27,640 --> 00:24:30,372
How do you think I feel after letting him
slip away right in front of me?

394
00:24:30,372 --> 00:24:31,776
No, I didn't mean that.

395
00:24:31,776 --> 00:24:34,716
The victim, Jang Eun Hak, is that person...

396
00:24:36,276 --> 00:24:38,344
Enough.

397
00:24:38,344 --> 00:24:41,572
What happened with those couple of
assault suspects from last time?

398
00:24:41,572 --> 00:24:43,548
Nothing yet on that one.

399
00:24:43,548 --> 00:24:45,783
The cybercrime unit
hasn't found anything either.

400
00:24:47,212 --> 00:24:49,956
So what are you going to do without me?

401
00:24:49,956 --> 00:24:52,376
What? Why would you be gone?

402
00:24:52,376 --> 00:24:54,076
Where are you going?

403
00:24:55,716 --> 00:24:57,392
[Civil Servant ID, Lee Dong Jin]

404
00:24:57,392 --> 00:24:58,984
You're getting a new mentor soon.

405
00:24:58,984 --> 00:25:03,349
Keep your eyes open
and learn everything you can.

406
00:25:04,788 --> 00:25:07,249
And don't make your previous mentor look bad.

407
00:25:11,256 --> 00:25:13,944
Wait, you're not quitting, are you?
You're not, right?

408
00:25:13,944 --> 00:25:15,900
Jeez, where are you going?

409
00:25:15,900 --> 00:25:17,744
I'm going to sleep.

410
00:25:17,744 --> 00:25:19,283
Now of all times?

411
00:25:19,283 --> 00:25:21,449
[Investigative Reporting Team]

412
00:25:21,449 --> 00:25:22,549
[Kwon Tae Seong]

413
00:25:22,549 --> 00:25:24,216
[Kingfisher, Search Results]

414
00:25:24,216 --> 00:25:25,949
[Kingfisher: Notorious Killer
or Avenger of Justice?]

415
00:25:27,049 --> 00:25:28,049
An avenger of justice...

416
00:25:28,049 --> 00:25:29,830
[Reporter Kwon Tae Seong
tracked the cases involving Kingfisher]

417
00:25:29,830 --> 00:25:31,116
[and found what they had in common]

418
00:25:32,583 --> 00:25:34,249
[Five Reflections on Kingfisher]

419
00:25:34,249 --> 00:25:37,783
[The Painful Questions Kingfisher
Forces Our Society to Ask]

420
00:25:38,649 --> 00:25:40,983
[Even if Kingfisher is caught tomorrow,
the questions he raised will remain]

421
00:25:40,983 --> 00:25:42,683
[Kwon Tae Seong, Social Affairs Reporter]

422
00:25:43,383 --> 00:25:45,668
Wow! As expected of Kwon Tae Seong.

423
00:25:45,668 --> 00:25:49,192
His comeback piece on Kingfisher
is an on-the-ground exclusive too.

424
00:25:49,192 --> 00:25:51,572
Ms. Gu, did you go there with him?

425
00:25:51,572 --> 00:25:54,664
Oh, no, I didn't know about it.

426
00:25:54,664 --> 00:25:57,788
Really? What? He acted like
he wasn't interested,

427
00:25:57,788 --> 00:26:00,160
but he was digging into it on his own?

428
00:26:00,160 --> 00:26:02,076
So it was all an act.

429
00:26:02,076 --> 00:26:03,144
But why isn't he here?

430
00:26:03,144 --> 00:26:05,316
We need a follow-up article fast.

431
00:26:08,616 --> 00:26:11,336
<i>Let's focus on the parole system
for our next piece.</i>

432
00:26:11,336 --> 00:26:15,408
<i>Let's look into possible loopholes
in Jang Eun Hak's parole review process,</i>

433
00:26:15,408 --> 00:26:18,852
<i>and focus on preventive measures
so this kind of thing doesn't happen again.</i>

434
00:26:18,852 --> 00:26:21,604
<i>Based on your research,
prepare a draft article.</i>

435
00:26:21,604 --> 00:26:22,849
<i>I have somewhere else I need to go today.</i>

436
00:26:22,849 --> 00:26:23,980
What's he saying? Why isn't he coming?

437
00:26:23,980 --> 00:26:26,800
Oh, I don't know about that.

438
00:26:26,800 --> 00:26:28,740
He just told me to prepare the article.

439
00:26:28,740 --> 00:26:32,076
Oh! A quick follow-up story? I like it.

440
00:26:32,076 --> 00:26:33,776
What's the angle?

441
00:26:35,624 --> 00:26:39,448
The homework Kingfisher left us?

442
00:26:39,448 --> 00:26:42,304
Oh, homework?

443
00:26:42,304 --> 00:26:44,004
What's that supposed to mean?

444
00:26:51,304 --> 00:26:53,004
Director Yoo

445
00:26:53,616 --> 00:26:57,344
must have been quite surprised
by her husband's article.

446
00:26:57,344 --> 00:26:59,116
She knew about it.

447
00:27:00,040 --> 00:27:03,748
- What?
- She fired, knowing her husband was coming.

448
00:27:03,748 --> 00:27:09,624
She probably figured that if she missed
the shot, more people might get hurt.

449
00:27:09,624 --> 00:27:13,464
What if she bumped into her husband?

450
00:27:13,464 --> 00:27:15,816
She probably factored all of that
into her decision.

451
00:27:16,716 --> 00:27:19,483
Because she has never once been wrong.

452
00:27:20,488 --> 00:27:24,076
She's never been wrong. Never made a mistake.

453
00:27:24,076 --> 00:27:27,848
Anyway, Assistant Manager Ki,
you must've had a hard time.

454
00:27:27,848 --> 00:27:32,712
I erased what I could
and checked for witnesses and vehicles,

455
00:27:32,712 --> 00:27:37,124
but the area was huge,
so I'm not sure we covered every route.

456
00:27:37,124 --> 00:27:40,376
We didn't get a chance to check
the new sniper position afterward, either.

457
00:27:40,376 --> 00:27:42,968
Getting out quickly was our priority.

458
00:27:42,968 --> 00:27:45,320
So now,

459
00:27:45,320 --> 00:27:48,360
we don't know where something
could come from, huh?

460
00:27:48,360 --> 00:27:52,276
So far, nothing concerning
has appeared in the police database.

461
00:27:52,276 --> 00:27:54,816
Keep monitoring it closely.

462
00:27:55,560 --> 00:27:59,336
And for the time being,
let's leave out the sniper stuff.

463
00:27:59,336 --> 00:28:01,096
Understood.

464
00:28:01,096 --> 00:28:02,796
Good work.

465
00:28:08,996 --> 00:28:11,248
Let's give you a bath, Tae Soon.

466
00:28:11,248 --> 00:28:14,972
You'll start to smell
if you don't get washed regularly.

467
00:28:14,972 --> 00:28:19,892
Yoo Bo Na must have had a great time,
like flying high, right?

468
00:28:19,892 --> 00:28:21,783
Shall we wash your hair too?

469
00:28:26,256 --> 00:28:30,472
Ah, you're so pretty.

470
00:28:30,472 --> 00:28:33,649
Nice and cool.

471
00:28:52,624 --> 00:28:54,416
Wow, look at all this dust.

472
00:28:56,100 --> 00:28:59,644
How can this be where our Director Yoo stays,
even for a minute?

473
00:28:59,644 --> 00:29:02,740
Jeez, move over there a bit!

474
00:29:02,740 --> 00:29:05,328
I'm going to get lung inflammation
from this, seriously.

475
00:29:05,328 --> 00:29:10,016
I can't sleep at night. I can't sleep.

476
00:29:11,788 --> 00:29:15,164
Our great Kingfisher
should be resting well today.

477
00:29:15,164 --> 00:29:18,088
But what is she doing?
Is she sleeping soundly?

478
00:29:18,088 --> 00:29:21,984
Even the way she sleeps must be totally cool.

479
00:29:21,984 --> 00:29:23,880
Oh, seriously, what are these?

480
00:29:23,880 --> 00:29:26,852
Keep this stuff cleaned up!

481
00:29:26,852 --> 00:29:28,849
Jeez.

482
00:29:28,849 --> 00:29:30,728
Ugh. What got on it, seriously?

483
00:29:30,728 --> 00:29:33,349
This is expensive,
and it can't even be dry-cleaned.

484
00:29:34,492 --> 00:29:36,984
How long has that trash been sitting here?

485
00:29:36,984 --> 00:29:39,816
Tae Soon, you got scared, didn't you?

486
00:29:41,549 --> 00:29:43,636
Are you really not going to help?

487
00:29:43,636 --> 00:29:45,336
Clean this up, now!

488
00:29:59,160 --> 00:30:01,488
Training's pretty intense today?

489
00:30:01,488 --> 00:30:04,216
You usually train like this
when you have a lot on your mind.

490
00:30:07,664 --> 00:30:10,480
I felt like my body was a bit stiff.

491
00:30:10,480 --> 00:30:14,049
Yesterday's mission was intense too.
You should get some rest.

492
00:30:18,208 --> 00:30:19,772
What about the shop?

493
00:30:19,772 --> 00:30:21,328
What if a customer comes?

494
00:30:21,328 --> 00:30:24,344
The only customers I have are flies.

495
00:30:24,344 --> 00:30:26,849
Guess I'll help you make a few more sales.

496
00:30:29,096 --> 00:30:32,116
Looks like your husband was at the scene.

497
00:30:33,680 --> 00:30:35,592
It's nothing you need to worry about.

498
00:30:35,592 --> 00:30:38,183
If it's work,
there's no reason for me to worry.

499
00:30:46,992 --> 00:30:49,428
Yul must have grown a lot lately.

500
00:30:49,428 --> 00:30:53,383
She's asking what her daddy does.

501
00:30:55,016 --> 00:31:00,516
I tell her, "Well, your daddy is someone
who does this kind of work."

502
00:31:03,049 --> 00:31:05,249
She may not understand now,

503
00:31:05,868 --> 00:31:08,148
but someday she will, right?

504
00:31:08,148 --> 00:31:10,628
What kind of person her daddy is.

505
00:31:10,628 --> 00:31:12,949
She'll be proud of him.

506
00:31:14,308 --> 00:31:17,649
That's the kind of work he does.

507
00:31:18,468 --> 00:31:21,083
It's when he's doing that work
that he really shines.

508
00:31:24,056 --> 00:31:29,483
He does his job, and I do mine.

509
00:31:31,232 --> 00:31:33,872
As for the unavoidable variables
that come up along the way...

510
00:31:33,872 --> 00:31:39,516
well, I'll manage them
just like I did in the field.

511
00:31:40,788 --> 00:31:43,268
Isn't that what you taught me?

512
00:31:43,268 --> 00:31:44,624
I did?

513
00:31:44,624 --> 00:31:49,283
Well, that was so long ago.
I barely remember.

514
00:31:55,092 --> 00:31:56,540
[Hye Ri's Mom]
<i>This is Hye Ri's mom.</i>

515
00:31:56,540 --> 00:31:58,684
<i>You got the call from the daycare, right?</i>

516
00:31:58,684 --> 00:32:01,768
<i>Don't you think we need to talk?</i>

517
00:32:01,768 --> 00:32:05,216
Why? What's the problem this time?

518
00:32:05,216 --> 00:32:09,196
[Yul's Daycare]

519
00:32:09,196 --> 00:32:11,649
Yes, Miss.

520
00:32:11,649 --> 00:32:13,349
Yul?

521
00:32:15,872 --> 00:32:17,816
Oh...

522
00:32:17,816 --> 00:32:19,549
Really?

523
00:32:38,316 --> 00:32:41,932
<i>Assistant Manager Ki, this is Kwon Se Ah.</i>

524
00:32:41,932 --> 00:32:44,640
<i>I got your number from Bo Na
and wanted to reach out.</i>

525
00:32:44,640 --> 00:32:47,780
<i>I'd like to return your cleaned clothes.</i>

526
00:32:47,780 --> 00:32:51,616
<i>When would be convenient?</i>

527
00:32:54,732 --> 00:32:56,549
<i>Just throw them...</i>

528
00:33:10,640 --> 00:33:12,649
<i>Let's meet after work today.</i>

529
00:33:14,608 --> 00:33:16,488
Today!

530
00:33:16,488 --> 00:33:18,216
Yeah!

531
00:33:18,216 --> 00:33:21,220
Hey, Kwon Se Ah! You can do this, right?

532
00:33:21,220 --> 00:33:22,383
Today's the day!

533
00:33:22,383 --> 00:33:25,883
He said let's meet today,
not tomorrow. What do I do?

534
00:33:26,652 --> 00:33:27,783
Oh?

535
00:33:27,783 --> 00:33:29,583
Oh, jeez.

536
00:33:31,400 --> 00:33:32,736
[Mr. Tiger]
<i>What are you doing now?</i>

537
00:33:32,736 --> 00:33:34,960
<i>I'm a little down today.
Let's just grab a meal.</i>

538
00:33:34,960 --> 00:33:36,660
What?

539
00:33:41,112 --> 00:33:43,228
<i>The customer's phone is turned off...</i>

540
00:33:43,228 --> 00:33:48,083
Seriously, where is he hiding
with his phone turned off?

541
00:33:48,749 --> 00:33:52,008
Was the shock of missing
Kingfisher too much for him?

542
00:33:52,008 --> 00:33:53,583
He's not really quitting, is he?

543
00:33:53,583 --> 00:33:56,183
[You have a new message]

544
00:33:57,949 --> 00:34:00,149
<i>Eat by yourself. I'm busy.</i>

545
00:34:01,696 --> 00:34:04,772
<i>Another date today?
With your sister-in-law again?</i>

546
00:34:04,772 --> 00:34:06,308
<i>No. Today it's with a guy.</i>

547
00:34:06,308 --> 00:34:07,720
Oh, with a guy.

548
00:34:07,720 --> 00:34:10,404
W-W-With a guy?

549
00:34:10,404 --> 00:34:12,104
With who?

550
00:34:17,916 --> 00:34:21,849
Yul, did something happen at kindergarten?

551
00:34:22,664 --> 00:34:24,364
Look at Mommy.

552
00:34:29,436 --> 00:34:32,664
Can you tell me what happened?

553
00:34:32,664 --> 00:34:35,476
That way, I can help you.

554
00:34:35,476 --> 00:34:39,640
Yul, I'm your best friend, remember?

555
00:34:39,640 --> 00:34:42,816
Best friends don't keep secrets
from each other.

556
00:34:43,968 --> 00:34:47,516
Mommy...

557
00:34:48,240 --> 00:34:49,868
Mommy.

558
00:34:49,868 --> 00:34:51,060
Oh, I see.

559
00:34:51,060 --> 00:34:53,820
Were you upset?

560
00:34:53,820 --> 00:34:56,816
Oh, dear. You were upset? Okay.

561
00:34:56,816 --> 00:34:59,349
I'm sorry. I understand.

562
00:35:02,256 --> 00:35:04,249
Mommy.

563
00:35:43,348 --> 00:35:47,149
<i>A punk who shot a dad dead</i>

564
00:35:48,032 --> 00:35:51,028
<i>right in front of his seven-year-old son.</i>

565
00:35:51,028 --> 00:35:56,324
<i>The kid was so traumatized
that he still can't speak.</i>

566
00:35:56,324 --> 00:36:01,804
A normal human being
wouldn't kill a parent in front of a child.

567
00:36:01,804 --> 00:36:06,216
No matter how vile the criminal was,
that still isn't right, right?

568
00:36:16,676 --> 00:36:19,060
What is it? What do you want?

569
00:36:19,060 --> 00:36:23,144
Does an elderly lady
and her grandson live here?

570
00:36:23,144 --> 00:36:24,849
An elderly lady?

571
00:36:25,544 --> 00:36:28,932
Oh, you must mean the people
who lived here before.

572
00:36:28,932 --> 00:36:31,583
I moved in last year.

573
00:36:33,152 --> 00:36:35,049
Okay, I see.

574
00:36:35,049 --> 00:36:36,768
[Ongsan Dream Real Estate]
Oh, that old lady?

575
00:36:36,768 --> 00:36:39,242
- She went to a nursing home last year.
- A nursing home?

576
00:36:39,242 --> 00:36:42,076
She had dementia or something
starting a few years ago.

577
00:36:42,076 --> 00:36:45,424
She's probably been a bit
in and out of it mentally for a while.

578
00:36:45,424 --> 00:36:49,304
Then what about the kid...
She had a grandson, didn't she?

579
00:36:49,304 --> 00:36:50,904
Her grandson?

580
00:36:50,904 --> 00:36:54,440
Oh, the boy who spoke strangely
and barely talked?

581
00:36:54,440 --> 00:36:59,384
Yeah. He'd been pretty troubled
ever since what happened to his dad.

582
00:36:59,384 --> 00:37:01,716
Do you happen to know where he is now?

583
00:37:01,716 --> 00:37:03,756
Didn't he end up in some kind of institution?

584
00:37:03,756 --> 00:37:05,276
Yeah, that's right.

585
00:37:05,276 --> 00:37:09,449
There was no one to take care of him,
so I think he went to an orphanage.

586
00:37:11,428 --> 00:37:13,172
Here.

587
00:37:13,172 --> 00:37:15,876
Sorry I'm returning these so late,
Assistant Manager Ki.

588
00:37:15,876 --> 00:37:18,383
They've been cleaned for a while,

589
00:37:18,383 --> 00:37:22,136
but I wasn't sure
how to get them back to you.

590
00:37:22,136 --> 00:37:23,836
Okay.

591
00:37:24,972 --> 00:37:26,672
Yeah.

592
00:37:28,528 --> 00:37:29,828
Don't you have anything else to say?

593
00:37:29,828 --> 00:37:31,380
Pardon?

594
00:37:31,380 --> 00:37:35,049
Oh, I guess it's my turn to talk.

595
00:37:35,916 --> 00:37:38,283
I believe we had a date planned.

596
00:37:40,788 --> 00:37:43,900
Oh, you remember.

597
00:37:43,900 --> 00:37:47,364
Then shall we start with dinner?

598
00:37:47,364 --> 00:37:49,064
I'm fine without eating.

599
00:37:54,988 --> 00:37:56,968
Hey, what are you doing here?

600
00:37:56,968 --> 00:37:59,572
You! Why are you here?
How did you know I was here?

601
00:37:59,572 --> 00:38:00,583
You told me.

602
00:38:00,583 --> 00:38:01,583
Huh?

603
00:38:01,583 --> 00:38:04,483
"Hey, where are you?" "Me? Yun Cafe."

604
00:38:04,483 --> 00:38:05,984
I've been looking everywhere for you.

605
00:38:05,984 --> 00:38:07,892
Why?

606
00:38:07,892 --> 00:38:10,848
Hello. I'm Beom Seong Hun,
Se Dol's friend here.

607
00:38:10,848 --> 00:38:12,044
I've heard a lot about you.

608
00:38:12,044 --> 00:38:14,149
Hey, what have I even said about him...

609
00:38:14,149 --> 00:38:15,149
No, I didn't.

610
00:38:15,149 --> 00:38:16,564
If it's not rude, may I join you?

611
00:38:16,564 --> 00:38:19,908
No, it is rude. It's very rude.
You're being incredibly rude.

612
00:38:19,908 --> 00:38:23,868
Oh, he might seem a bit clueless,
but he's definitely not a bad guy.

613
00:38:23,868 --> 00:38:26,852
First of all, his job is a cop.

614
00:38:26,852 --> 00:38:29,349
Can't you see this isn't exactly
the place for you right now?

615
00:38:29,349 --> 00:38:32,576
Why don't you leave while I'm asking nicely?

616
00:38:32,576 --> 00:38:34,952
Hey, why isn't this the place for me?

617
00:38:34,952 --> 00:38:36,592
Don't you know the world is
a dangerous place these days?

618
00:38:36,592 --> 00:38:37,905
Even if he looks innocent on the outside,

619
00:38:37,905 --> 00:38:41,250
an expert like me needs to scan him
and see if he's rotten on the inside.

620
00:38:41,250 --> 00:38:42,783
You, seriously...

621
00:38:43,780 --> 00:38:47,704
Not that I'm saying that's what you are,
of course. Don't get me wrong.

622
00:38:47,704 --> 00:38:51,349
We were just about to
go get something to eat.

623
00:38:52,304 --> 00:38:54,644
Shall we get going?

624
00:38:54,644 --> 00:38:55,836
Oh, food!

625
00:38:55,836 --> 00:38:56,983
Hey, perfect timing.

626
00:38:56,983 --> 00:38:59,272
I was just getting hungry.

627
00:38:59,272 --> 00:39:02,416
Well, since we've met like this,
why don't we have a meal together?

628
00:39:02,416 --> 00:39:03,596
I know a good place nearby.

629
00:39:03,596 --> 00:39:07,312
Assistant Manager Ki, we'll go ahead.
Can you come out in a little while?

630
00:39:07,312 --> 00:39:08,736
Sure.

631
00:39:08,736 --> 00:39:10,449
- Come on out!
- Hey.

632
00:39:13,456 --> 00:39:14,536
Oh, seriously.

633
00:39:14,536 --> 00:39:17,764
Hey, put this down.

634
00:39:17,764 --> 00:39:19,644
Hey, do you have a gun on you right now?

635
00:39:19,644 --> 00:39:21,108
Do you think I would? What's with the gun?

636
00:39:21,108 --> 00:39:23,183
So I can blow your head off!

637
00:39:23,183 --> 00:39:25,083
Hey, that hurts!

638
00:39:25,856 --> 00:39:26,908
I came because I was worried about you, okay?

639
00:39:26,908 --> 00:39:29,016
About what?

640
00:39:29,016 --> 00:39:30,964
You know I've got good instincts, right?

641
00:39:30,964 --> 00:39:33,476
Oh, you do? You do?

642
00:39:33,476 --> 00:39:36,349
There's something off about that guy.

643
00:39:36,349 --> 00:39:38,488
Like he reeks of a brutal crime or something?

644
00:39:38,488 --> 00:39:40,683
He's my sister-in-law's coworker, got it?

645
00:39:41,888 --> 00:39:45,616
Then that whole company sounds suspicious.

646
00:39:45,616 --> 00:39:47,164
Hmm...

647
00:39:47,164 --> 00:39:49,584
If you don't have a gun,
I'll use my bare hands, you punk!

648
00:39:49,584 --> 00:39:51,216
Why did you come here? Aren't you leaving?

649
00:39:51,216 --> 00:39:53,949
Why'd you come here just to piss me off?

650
00:39:53,949 --> 00:39:56,216
- Hey, that's enough.
- Where is it?

651
00:39:57,584 --> 00:39:58,912
That restaurant.

652
00:39:58,912 --> 00:40:00,612
What?

653
00:40:07,416 --> 00:40:11,040
This is the kind of chicken feet place
you can't quit once you've tried it.

654
00:40:11,040 --> 00:40:13,793
Alright, starting with
whole chicken feet, spicy chicken feet,

655
00:40:13,793 --> 00:40:15,192
boneless chicken feet,
and braised chicken feet.

656
00:40:15,192 --> 00:40:17,664
For the record, our usual move
is to start with the soupy ones

657
00:40:17,664 --> 00:40:19,583
and finish with the grilled spicy ones.

658
00:40:19,583 --> 00:40:21,136
Do you like chicken feet?

659
00:40:21,136 --> 00:40:23,483
Sometimes. Very occasionally.

660
00:40:23,483 --> 00:40:26,483
They're also packed with collagen, you know.

661
00:40:29,924 --> 00:40:31,068
Can't you eat them?

662
00:40:31,068 --> 00:40:34,683
No. I'm going to give them
a try starting today.

663
00:40:34,683 --> 00:40:36,483
Then please enjoy.

664
00:40:46,184 --> 00:40:47,884
Cheers!

665
00:40:51,572 --> 00:40:53,272
Cheers!

666
00:40:55,988 --> 00:40:57,124
This is so good.

667
00:40:57,124 --> 00:41:00,249
You said you're a cop. What division?

668
00:41:01,344 --> 00:41:03,349
Criminal Affairs, Violent Crimes.

669
00:41:04,076 --> 00:41:06,348
Oh, Violent Crimes.

670
00:41:06,348 --> 00:41:09,416
You must get some interesting cases.

671
00:41:09,416 --> 00:41:11,064
Plenty of horrible ones.

672
00:41:11,064 --> 00:41:13,256
People die, get hurt, get messed up.

673
00:41:13,256 --> 00:41:16,216
What case have you been working on lately?

674
00:41:18,016 --> 00:41:20,228
That's confidential.

675
00:41:20,228 --> 00:41:24,516
You seem really interested in crime, though?

676
00:41:25,560 --> 00:41:27,764
I'm interested in profiling.

677
00:41:27,764 --> 00:41:30,116
I majored in psychology too.

678
00:41:31,149 --> 00:41:33,568
You majored in psychology.

679
00:41:33,568 --> 00:41:35,283
That's impressive.

680
00:41:35,936 --> 00:41:38,183
Then let me give you a scenario.

681
00:41:38,183 --> 00:41:40,749
Want to try profiling it for fun?

682
00:41:41,836 --> 00:41:43,952
Sounds fun.

683
00:41:43,952 --> 00:41:46,124
Okay, a man

684
00:41:46,124 --> 00:41:49,716
was shot dead through a gap
in a motel window by a sniper rifle.

685
00:41:50,388 --> 00:41:52,240
Who's the killer?

686
00:41:52,240 --> 00:41:54,364
Are you kidding? The whole country knows.

687
00:41:54,364 --> 00:41:55,500
It happened yesterday too.

688
00:41:55,500 --> 00:41:57,408
Hey, do you think I'd ask about that?

689
00:41:57,408 --> 00:42:00,916
Who do you think Kingfisher really is?

690
00:42:01,924 --> 00:42:03,624
I'm not sure.

691
00:42:04,696 --> 00:42:09,049
The police don't have enough evidence
to make an inference like that.

692
00:42:09,983 --> 00:42:14,900
The whole process is extremely methodical,
and he leaves no evidence behind.

693
00:42:14,900 --> 00:42:18,083
That's why I have a theory.

694
00:42:18,083 --> 00:42:22,816
"Maybe Kingfisher isn't acting alone?"
That kind of.

695
00:42:24,596 --> 00:42:26,108
That's possible.

696
00:42:26,108 --> 00:42:28,516
His methods do seem highly organized.

697
00:42:29,744 --> 00:42:33,283
But you sound pretty certain, though?

698
00:42:35,476 --> 00:42:38,083
That he never leaves any evidence.

699
00:42:38,716 --> 00:42:41,049
That's why the police
haven't caught him yet, right?

700
00:42:41,748 --> 00:42:44,236
Ma'am, one more order of
chicken feet in broth, please.

701
00:42:44,236 --> 00:42:46,040
Yeah.

702
00:42:46,040 --> 00:42:47,383
Hey!

703
00:42:47,383 --> 00:42:49,504
Did you really eat all that
by yourself already?

704
00:42:49,504 --> 00:42:51,572
Me?

705
00:42:51,572 --> 00:42:53,272
Oh, my.

706
00:42:59,136 --> 00:43:01,849
Wait, you've got something on you.

707
00:43:12,184 --> 00:43:14,492
Thank you.

708
00:43:14,492 --> 00:43:16,949
It's nice to see someone
with such a good appetite.

709
00:43:20,083 --> 00:43:23,316
I usually eat pretty well.

710
00:43:23,316 --> 00:43:25,683
Assistant Manager Ki,
you should eat some too.

711
00:43:25,683 --> 00:43:28,772
Oh, I'm fine. I don't really eat that much.

712
00:43:28,772 --> 00:43:29,896
Oh, right.

713
00:43:29,896 --> 00:43:32,516
You did say you don't eat much, right?

714
00:43:33,396 --> 00:43:35,172
I should get going.

715
00:43:35,172 --> 00:43:36,349
I need to head back to the station.

716
00:43:36,349 --> 00:43:37,624
Yeah? You sure?

717
00:43:37,624 --> 00:43:39,272
Go ahead, bye.

718
00:43:39,272 --> 00:43:41,112
Don't forget to pay on your way out.

719
00:43:41,112 --> 00:43:43,464
Yeah, just stay and have some fun.

720
00:43:43,464 --> 00:43:46,016
Maybe we'll see each other again sometime.

721
00:43:59,292 --> 00:44:02,916
Wow! Looks like Se Dol
finally escaped the single life.

722
00:44:04,480 --> 00:44:07,683
Jeez, but why do I feel like this?

723
00:44:13,796 --> 00:44:16,949
Wow, one beer here costs...

724
00:44:16,949 --> 00:44:18,983
Is this some fancy place?

725
00:44:19,632 --> 00:44:22,583
Everyone, let's be prepared.

726
00:44:22,583 --> 00:44:26,049
We need to nip this in the bud.

727
00:44:32,704 --> 00:44:35,048
Both of you are here as well.

728
00:44:35,048 --> 00:44:37,349
Thanks for showing up.

729
00:44:39,284 --> 00:44:41,956
This isn't just about Hye Ri.

730
00:44:41,956 --> 00:44:46,904
Who knows whose child could be next?

731
00:44:46,904 --> 00:44:50,183
I ordered some beer and snacks. Is beer okay?

732
00:44:50,183 --> 00:44:52,988
Oh, absolutely. Beer sounds great.

733
00:44:52,988 --> 00:44:57,196
Well, since we're at a bar,
we might as well have a drink.

734
00:44:57,196 --> 00:44:59,260
What are you talking about, beer?

735
00:44:59,260 --> 00:45:02,544
We left the kids at home,
so let's keep this short and wrap it up.

736
00:45:02,544 --> 00:45:07,300
Just because of some stupid blocks,
those two kids ganged up and hurt Hye Ri.

737
00:45:07,300 --> 00:45:10,132
She must've been so upset.

738
00:45:10,132 --> 00:45:12,916
She came home and wouldn't even
eat her favorite pork cutlet...

739
00:45:14,704 --> 00:45:16,240
Oh, my.

740
00:45:16,240 --> 00:45:18,880
What's this?

741
00:45:18,880 --> 00:45:21,683
Is that Yul's finger?

742
00:45:22,592 --> 00:45:24,940
Oh, my God. What happened?

743
00:45:24,940 --> 00:45:27,332
Every time Seo Jun built something
with the blocks,

744
00:45:27,332 --> 00:45:28,848
Hye Ri would come and knock it down.

745
00:45:28,848 --> 00:45:32,283
So Yul tried to stop her.

746
00:45:32,283 --> 00:45:36,516
Then Hye Ri bit Yul's finger.

747
00:45:37,632 --> 00:45:41,652
Seo Jun got scared and pushed Hye Ri away.

748
00:45:41,652 --> 00:45:44,420
As far as he's concerned,
he was only trying to separate them.

749
00:45:44,420 --> 00:45:48,308
Wait, Hye Ri bit Yul?

750
00:45:48,308 --> 00:45:49,936
Hye Ri didn't mention any of that.

751
00:45:49,936 --> 00:45:54,580
Oh, maybe she was afraid you'd scold her,
so she didn't tell you.

752
00:45:54,580 --> 00:45:57,404
Oh, that must've hurt.

753
00:45:57,404 --> 00:46:02,583
Why didn't Yul tell the teacher about this?

754
00:46:04,204 --> 00:46:05,204
Wait.

755
00:46:05,204 --> 00:46:08,868
So did you call us here
to complain about this?

756
00:46:08,868 --> 00:46:11,316
To get an apology out of me?

757
00:46:12,352 --> 00:46:14,583
Hye Ri's mom.

758
00:46:14,583 --> 00:46:16,083
Yeah?

759
00:46:16,083 --> 00:46:19,716
No, why? What is it?

760
00:46:20,720 --> 00:46:25,983
As a mom, what am I supposed
to do in a situation like this...

761
00:46:27,256 --> 00:46:29,412
I honestly don't know.

762
00:46:29,412 --> 00:46:33,183
So I just told Yul what felt right to me.

763
00:46:33,183 --> 00:46:35,177
I told Yul that Hye Ri didn't do it
because she hated Yul.

764
00:46:35,177 --> 00:46:37,883
She was probably just upset for a moment.

765
00:46:42,908 --> 00:46:47,036
Well, the kids still have to
live together going forward.

766
00:46:47,036 --> 00:46:49,532
We need to comfort them
so this doesn't leave a bad memory,

767
00:46:49,532 --> 00:46:54,382
and help them get along better from now on.

768
00:46:54,382 --> 00:46:58,849
I think that's what adults should do.

769
00:46:59,468 --> 00:47:04,792
So I wanted to ask for your advice
on how to do that.

770
00:47:04,792 --> 00:47:06,556
Oh, what is there to do?

771
00:47:06,556 --> 00:47:09,716
Just discipline them
if they did something wrong,

772
00:47:09,716 --> 00:47:14,812
have them apologize if they need to,
and let the moms clear the air. That's all.

773
00:47:14,812 --> 00:47:16,281
- That's right.
- Yeah.

774
00:47:16,281 --> 00:47:18,212
Right.

775
00:47:18,212 --> 00:47:20,549
Oh, the drinks are here.

776
00:47:24,600 --> 00:47:26,300
Thank you.

777
00:47:27,664 --> 00:47:30,232
Oh, you made it?

778
00:47:30,232 --> 00:47:32,249
Sorry I'm late.

779
00:47:34,012 --> 00:47:35,980
Just a second.

780
00:47:35,980 --> 00:47:39,216
Oh, I saw some blood earlier,
and I'm still feeling queasy.

781
00:47:48,383 --> 00:47:50,268
Hye Ri's mom is...

782
00:47:50,268 --> 00:47:52,008
- Over here.
- Here.

783
00:47:52,008 --> 00:47:54,260
Oh, there you are.

784
00:47:54,260 --> 00:47:58,049
Hye Ri's mom, I heard
our Seo Jun pushed Hye Ri.

785
00:47:58,049 --> 00:48:01,056
That little punk.

786
00:48:01,056 --> 00:48:04,728
I'll give him a good talking-to
when I get home.

787
00:48:04,728 --> 00:48:06,900
I'll make him write an apology letter too.

788
00:48:06,900 --> 00:48:10,016
But I heard he already apologized to Hye Ri.

789
00:48:10,620 --> 00:48:12,172
Yes, he did.

790
00:48:12,172 --> 00:48:14,984
Yes, he apologized.

791
00:48:14,984 --> 00:48:16,816
Well, that's good.

792
00:48:18,392 --> 00:48:20,673
I'll apologize too, on behalf of his mom.

793
00:48:20,673 --> 00:48:23,083
- Well...
- I'm sorry, Hye Ri's mom.

794
00:48:24,112 --> 00:48:25,883
Wow!

795
00:48:25,883 --> 00:48:29,383
That's a bold apology.

796
00:48:34,994 --> 00:48:36,694
I...

797
00:48:39,376 --> 00:48:41,076
Sor...

798
00:48:42,428 --> 00:48:44,120
What should I do?

799
00:48:44,120 --> 00:48:47,149
Do you think Yul will be okay
without going to the hospital?

800
00:48:49,856 --> 00:48:53,440
Oh, it went down pretty quickly
after I put some medicine on it.

801
00:48:53,440 --> 00:48:54,848
Thanks for asking.

802
00:48:54,848 --> 00:48:57,449
- Oh, good.
- What a relief.

803
00:48:58,588 --> 00:49:00,800
Wow, this is great, right?

804
00:49:00,800 --> 00:49:04,456
Let's have a proper drink
and loosen up. Cheers.

805
00:49:04,456 --> 00:49:06,200
- Out of drinks.
- Oh, no beer.

806
00:49:06,200 --> 00:49:07,572
Can I have a glass of beer?

807
00:49:07,572 --> 00:49:10,449
- Here, you can have some of mine for now.
- Okay, sure.

808
00:49:13,476 --> 00:49:15,084
Cheers.

809
00:49:15,084 --> 00:49:17,416
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

810
00:49:24,819 --> 00:49:26,200
Well...

811
00:49:26,200 --> 00:49:30,776
Assistant Manager Ki,
did I happen to do something wrong?

812
00:49:30,776 --> 00:49:32,476
Not at all.

813
00:49:33,332 --> 00:49:37,756
You just seem pretty different from
how you were at the restaurant.

814
00:49:37,756 --> 00:49:40,160
You haven't said much at all.

815
00:49:40,160 --> 00:49:42,828
This is the real me.
Earlier, I was putting on an act.

816
00:49:42,828 --> 00:49:45,400
Why would you do that?

817
00:49:45,400 --> 00:49:46,460
Do you like me?

818
00:49:46,460 --> 00:49:48,416
Yeah, I mean, no.

819
00:49:53,164 --> 00:49:54,500
Yeah.

820
00:49:54,500 --> 00:49:57,328
I'm sorry, but I have no interest in you.

821
00:49:57,328 --> 00:49:59,183
You're not my type.

822
00:50:00,012 --> 00:50:02,088
I'm sorry for asking you out.

823
00:50:02,088 --> 00:50:04,088
It was way too impulsive.

824
00:50:04,088 --> 00:50:05,976
Sorry.

825
00:50:05,976 --> 00:50:08,716
That's what I wanted to tell you,
so I asked to see you today.

826
00:50:11,884 --> 00:50:16,024
Then what is your type?

827
00:50:16,024 --> 00:50:17,724
I'm...

828
00:50:20,436 --> 00:50:23,516
<i>attracted to a woman strong enough
to hold my life in her hands.</i>

829
00:50:23,516 --> 00:50:25,232
Eat up and relax, rookie.

830
00:50:25,232 --> 00:50:27,640
<i>A woman who could hurt me at any time,</i>

831
00:50:27,640 --> 00:50:29,516
but chooses not to.

832
00:50:31,749 --> 00:50:35,049
That's quite a unique preference.

833
00:50:38,204 --> 00:50:41,988
But Assistant Manager Ki,
you don't even know me.

834
00:50:41,988 --> 00:50:43,960
That's right.

835
00:50:43,960 --> 00:50:46,283
And I don't particularly want to know you.

836
00:50:51,416 --> 00:50:53,048
Okay!

837
00:50:53,048 --> 00:50:55,849
Found today's punching bag.

838
00:50:55,849 --> 00:50:57,849
- Found one.
- Found one.

839
00:51:04,249 --> 00:51:06,549
[Cybercrime Unit, Sergeant Kim]

840
00:51:09,524 --> 00:51:11,788
- Yes, Mr. Kim.
- Hey, Mr. Beom. It's me.

841
00:51:11,788 --> 00:51:13,432
Guess what I found?

842
00:51:13,432 --> 00:51:14,849
I sent you a link.
Can you check it right away?

843
00:51:14,849 --> 00:51:17,549
Sure. Give me a second.

844
00:51:22,540 --> 00:51:24,783
<i>Hello, gentlemen!</i>

845
00:51:24,783 --> 00:51:27,483
- <i>It's time for Mace Man's justice.</i>
- <i>Justice!</i>

846
00:51:27,483 --> 00:51:30,464
<i>Let's get things started with a bang.</i>

847
00:51:30,464 --> 00:51:31,464
What's this?

848
00:51:31,464 --> 00:51:33,849
Apparently, it's a streaming site
that's been growing underground lately.

849
00:51:33,849 --> 00:51:36,612
They livestream violent or obscene videos,

850
00:51:36,612 --> 00:51:38,056
and apparently get paid in
some kind of cryptocurrency.

851
00:51:38,056 --> 00:51:42,636
<i>Who are we going to teach a lesson today?</i>

852
00:51:42,636 --> 00:51:44,216
<i>Let's go with a pretty one, if possible.</i>

853
00:51:44,216 --> 00:51:46,456
<i>You won't be able to see their faces
once they're covered in blood, idiot.</i>

854
00:51:46,456 --> 00:51:48,488
See them? Three masked men.

855
00:51:48,488 --> 00:51:51,636
These guys look like the couple-assault
suspects you've been after, right?

856
00:51:51,636 --> 00:51:54,216
Oh, you're right.

857
00:51:54,216 --> 00:51:57,332
Man, so cryptocurrency was their motive?

858
00:51:57,332 --> 00:51:58,540
Does it show where they are?

859
00:51:58,540 --> 00:51:59,824
It says Songju Park.

860
00:51:59,824 --> 00:52:01,120
Songju Park?

861
00:52:01,120 --> 00:52:02,649
Huh? That's nearby.

862
00:52:02,649 --> 00:52:05,944
<i>So what do you think of
these punks, gentlemen?</i>

863
00:52:05,944 --> 00:52:08,449
<i>Zoom in on the woman's face.</i>

864
00:52:08,449 --> 00:52:10,972
<i>Let's see.</i>

865
00:52:10,972 --> 00:52:13,184
- Huh?
- <i>There.</i>

866
00:52:13,184 --> 00:52:14,340
Darn it.

867
00:52:14,340 --> 00:52:16,040
Ah, well...

868
00:52:16,904 --> 00:52:19,596
Mr. Kim, please call for backup
from the local precinct,

869
00:52:19,596 --> 00:52:21,083
and send ambulances to Songju Park.

870
00:52:21,083 --> 00:52:22,552
- Three ambulances.
- Three?

871
00:52:22,552 --> 00:52:26,148
- Not two?
- No, three. Make sure it's three.

872
00:52:26,148 --> 00:52:29,304
No. Kwon Se Ah, please!

873
00:52:29,304 --> 00:52:31,004
This way, right?

874
00:52:31,624 --> 00:52:33,332
What are they doing?

875
00:52:33,332 --> 00:52:34,892
Why are they just walking?

876
00:52:34,892 --> 00:52:37,604
The guy's obviously a pathetic loser.

877
00:52:37,604 --> 00:52:40,072
He can't even hold her hand.

878
00:52:40,072 --> 00:52:45,949
Well, gentlemen,
I think it's time to teach them a lesson.

879
00:52:48,212 --> 00:52:49,677
I've already been rejected,

880
00:52:49,677 --> 00:52:52,549
but since I started this confession anyway,
let me just finish it.

881
00:52:53,844 --> 00:52:58,824
The first day we met,
when you said you'd help me find Yul,

882
00:52:58,824 --> 00:53:03,352
that's when you dove straight into my heart.

883
00:53:03,352 --> 00:53:05,052
And...

884
00:53:07,420 --> 00:53:09,120
Who on earth are you?

885
00:53:10,444 --> 00:53:12,144
Wait...

886
00:53:14,488 --> 00:53:16,916
Assistant Manager Ki, are you okay?

887
00:53:19,296 --> 00:53:21,116
<i>I'm...</i>

888
00:53:21,116 --> 00:53:24,476
<i>attracted to a woman strong enough
to hold my life in her hands.</i>

889
00:53:24,476 --> 00:53:27,500
<i>A woman who could hurt me at any time,</i>

890
00:53:27,500 --> 00:53:28,683
<i>but chooses not to.</i>

891
00:53:28,683 --> 00:53:31,369
[Kwon Se Ah, Current: Graduate student,
College of Physical Education]

892
00:53:31,369 --> 00:53:33,260
[Former: Women's Judo National Team Reserve]

893
00:53:33,260 --> 00:53:34,588
Kwon Se Ah, please.

894
00:53:34,588 --> 00:53:38,049
Take it easy. Don't kill them.

895
00:53:40,932 --> 00:53:42,683
Assistant Manager Ki!

896
00:53:42,683 --> 00:53:46,492
Yeah, I'm... I'm fine.

897
00:53:46,492 --> 00:53:47,916
Oh, no, what do I do?

898
00:53:47,916 --> 00:53:50,616
I'm sorry. Are you okay?

899
00:53:50,616 --> 00:53:52,188
Oh, dear.

900
00:53:52,188 --> 00:53:54,332
Oh, please don't come any closer.

901
00:53:54,332 --> 00:53:57,416
Please, just stay back.

902
00:54:00,129 --> 00:54:03,349
Oh, my tailbone... Oh...

903
00:54:03,349 --> 00:54:06,200
Jeez, I said stay back.

904
00:54:06,200 --> 00:54:08,683
Oh, my, are you okay?

905
00:54:08,683 --> 00:54:10,276
Oh...

906
00:54:10,276 --> 00:54:12,549
Stay still! Don't move!

907
00:54:12,549 --> 00:54:14,420
Darn, this is so embarrassing.

908
00:54:14,420 --> 00:54:16,412
Hey, take out that punk first!

909
00:54:16,412 --> 00:54:19,149
If you keep doing this,
I'm seriously going to call the police...

910
00:54:27,296 --> 00:54:29,716
No time for that.

911
00:54:31,720 --> 00:54:34,028
Oh, I'm terrified.

912
00:54:34,028 --> 00:54:37,349
Assistant Manager Ki,
that must've scared you, right?

913
00:54:40,749 --> 00:54:43,283
It... did.

914
00:54:44,388 --> 00:54:45,736
They just came out of nowhere.

915
00:54:45,736 --> 00:54:47,016
Hey, Kwon Se Ah!

916
00:54:47,016 --> 00:54:48,016
Huh? What?

917
00:54:48,016 --> 00:54:49,276
Hey, you!

918
00:54:49,276 --> 00:54:51,296
You...

919
00:54:51,296 --> 00:54:52,924
I knew you'd pull something like this.

920
00:54:52,924 --> 00:54:54,496
Huh?

921
00:54:54,496 --> 00:54:56,120
Hey!

922
00:54:56,120 --> 00:54:58,896
Hey, look at what you've done to him...

923
00:54:58,896 --> 00:55:01,679
I told you not to use
your techniques carelessly, right?

924
00:55:01,679 --> 00:55:04,740
Well... It just happened automatically.

925
00:55:04,740 --> 00:55:07,096
Hey, wake up!

926
00:55:07,096 --> 00:55:10,240
Are you okay? Hey!

927
00:55:10,240 --> 00:55:13,248
Wow, he passed out cold.

928
00:55:13,248 --> 00:55:15,536
Okay, no visible injuries.

929
00:55:15,536 --> 00:55:17,284
And you're not hurt anywhere, right?
Of course not.

930
00:55:17,284 --> 00:55:19,312
- Yeah.
- And you...

931
00:55:19,312 --> 00:55:22,116
barely had to lift a finger anyway.

932
00:55:32,176 --> 00:55:34,616
Oh, nice timing.

933
00:55:36,049 --> 00:55:38,049
[Beom Seong Hun, Current:
Nambu Station's Youngest Detective]

934
00:55:38,049 --> 00:55:40,049
[Former: Asian Games Gold Medalist
in Men's Judo, Special Police Hire]

935
00:55:40,049 --> 00:55:41,576
Don't move.

936
00:55:41,576 --> 00:55:46,412
You're under arrest for aggravated assault
and obstruction of official duties.

937
00:55:46,412 --> 00:55:50,232
You have the right
to remain silent and to an attorney.

938
00:55:50,232 --> 00:55:52,616
Oh, right. And anything stupid you say
can be used against you,

939
00:55:52,616 --> 00:55:54,616
so watch what you say.

940
00:55:56,249 --> 00:55:59,416
Mr. Tiger! True colors of a cop!
Champions of justice!

941
00:55:59,416 --> 00:56:00,676
- Hey!
- Hey!

942
00:56:00,676 --> 00:56:03,683
- Take them down and finish it!
- Take them down and finish it!

943
00:56:03,683 --> 00:56:05,149
- You remember?
- Hey, how do you know that?

944
00:56:05,149 --> 00:56:07,556
- This is nothing.
- Hey, what's going on here?

945
00:56:07,556 --> 00:56:09,504
- A throw.
- Hey, that's not right!

946
00:56:09,504 --> 00:56:11,308
No, you do it from here, like this!

947
00:56:11,308 --> 00:56:12,549
- Bam!
- Oh!

948
00:56:12,549 --> 00:56:15,692
What was that? Wow, you're good.

949
00:56:15,692 --> 00:56:18,204
- Of course, I'm a cop.
- Jeez.

950
00:56:18,204 --> 00:56:20,649
The police will be here soon...

951
00:56:22,864 --> 00:56:24,564
The kid...

952
00:56:25,264 --> 00:56:28,144
She's getting harder and harder to handle.

953
00:56:28,144 --> 00:56:31,864
Of course. The older they get,
the less they listen.

954
00:56:31,864 --> 00:56:35,512
I complained to my mom once,
and you know what she said?

955
00:56:35,512 --> 00:56:36,940
Did she say she'd scold your kid?

956
00:56:36,940 --> 00:56:39,849
She said my kid's
exactly like I was as a kid.

957
00:56:41,248 --> 00:56:44,683
She prayed for me
to have a daughter just like me,

958
00:56:45,948 --> 00:56:48,524
and her wish came true.

959
00:56:48,524 --> 00:56:50,616
That scared me more than anything.

960
00:56:50,616 --> 00:56:52,760
"A daughter who takes after me."

961
00:56:52,760 --> 00:56:56,264
Kids are half born that way
and half learn by watching.

962
00:56:56,264 --> 00:57:01,076
That's why they say,
"A child is a reflection of their parents."

963
00:57:01,076 --> 00:57:04,272
That saying, that one really hits me hard.

964
00:57:04,272 --> 00:57:07,032
I mean, isn't that a little unfair to me?

965
00:57:07,032 --> 00:57:12,216
All the time and effort I put into her...

966
00:57:13,896 --> 00:57:15,960
Jeez.

967
00:57:15,960 --> 00:57:17,288
Hold on.

968
00:57:17,288 --> 00:57:19,920
- It's your husband.
- Your husband.

969
00:57:19,920 --> 00:57:21,620
What?

970
00:57:22,416 --> 00:57:24,383
What time is it right now?

971
00:57:24,383 --> 00:57:26,824
Look at the clock.

972
00:57:26,824 --> 00:57:29,620
You come home at midnight every day,

973
00:57:29,620 --> 00:57:33,984
and you're complaining about
having to watch the kid one day early?

974
00:57:33,984 --> 00:57:35,416
What, her bath?

975
00:57:35,416 --> 00:57:39,104
Just give her a bath yourself.

976
00:57:39,104 --> 00:57:42,416
I don't know. Just put her to bed.

977
00:57:43,392 --> 00:57:45,316
Or whatever.

978
00:57:46,036 --> 00:57:49,472
Seriously, how is he exactly like my husband?

979
00:57:49,472 --> 00:57:50,916
We had this kid together,

980
00:57:50,916 --> 00:57:55,296
so why am I the one expected to do
all the parenting?

981
00:57:55,296 --> 00:57:56,676
If this is how it's going to be,

982
00:57:56,676 --> 00:57:58,468
he shouldn't have been begging
for a second kid.

983
00:57:58,468 --> 00:58:00,240
Well, my husband,

984
00:58:00,240 --> 00:58:03,612
even when I beg him to play
with the kids instead of drinking,

985
00:58:03,612 --> 00:58:06,056
all he ever says is, "Yeah, yeah."

986
00:58:06,056 --> 00:58:07,849
And one time,

987
00:58:08,780 --> 00:58:10,409
he called saying he was leaving,

988
00:58:10,409 --> 00:58:11,976
and then he took so long to show up
that I went down to check,

989
00:58:11,976 --> 00:58:14,983
and there he was, sleeping
in the parking lot. This guy, seriously.

990
00:58:14,983 --> 00:58:15,983
In the car?

991
00:58:15,983 --> 00:58:17,308
Yeah.

992
00:58:17,308 --> 00:58:18,828
What a gentleman.

993
00:58:18,828 --> 00:58:20,004
What?

994
00:58:20,004 --> 00:58:23,020
I got a call from the security office
once about Hye Ri's dad.

995
00:58:23,020 --> 00:58:25,183
They said he was snoring
away in the elevator.

996
00:58:25,183 --> 00:58:26,216
Oh, God.

997
00:58:26,216 --> 00:58:29,683
What if the kids learn from watching them?

998
00:58:30,688 --> 00:58:33,916
Then just raise them alone as I do.

999
00:58:41,172 --> 00:58:42,724
What about you, Yul's mom?

1000
00:58:42,724 --> 00:58:44,520
What?

1001
00:58:44,520 --> 00:58:46,132
Yul's dad.

1002
00:58:46,132 --> 00:58:48,240
I'm curious what kind of dad Yul has.

1003
00:58:48,240 --> 00:58:51,149
Yeah, me too. What's he like?

1004
00:58:52,628 --> 00:58:54,649
My husband?

1005
00:59:00,220 --> 00:59:01,868
Did my little girl get hurt a lot?

1006
00:59:01,868 --> 00:59:04,560
Yeah, it hurt a lot.

1007
00:59:04,560 --> 00:59:09,312
It's okay. I put some medicine on it,
so it'll get better soon.

1008
00:59:09,312 --> 00:59:12,949
What made you the saddest today, Yul?

1009
00:59:14,476 --> 00:59:16,316
Hye Ri cried today.

1010
00:59:16,316 --> 00:59:18,936
Oh, did seeing Hye Ri cry
make you the saddest?

1011
00:59:18,936 --> 00:59:22,128
- Yeah.
- Why did that make you so sad?

1012
00:59:22,128 --> 00:59:27,416
Because Mommy told me
to get along with my friends.

1013
00:59:27,416 --> 00:59:32,248
Oh, you wanted to get along
with your friend, but it didn't work out?

1014
00:59:32,248 --> 00:59:35,904
Yeah. But we shouldn't hurt our friends.

1015
00:59:35,904 --> 00:59:38,004
That's right. We shouldn't hurt our friends.

1016
00:59:38,004 --> 00:59:42,204
- No biting and no pushing, right?
- Yeah.

1017
00:59:42,204 --> 00:59:46,554
But sometimes things like that happen
when you're playing with friends.

1018
00:59:46,554 --> 00:59:47,780
What should you do then?

1019
00:59:47,780 --> 00:59:49,392
I should say "Sorry."

1020
00:59:49,392 --> 00:59:50,392
That's right.

1021
00:59:50,392 --> 00:59:54,672
Apologize, make up, and be friends again.

1022
00:59:54,672 --> 00:59:57,388
Yeah, I'll give them presents
and ask them to play with me.

1023
00:59:57,388 --> 01:00:00,132
Wow, your friends are going to love that.

1024
01:00:00,132 --> 01:00:03,780
Then how about we pick out presents
for your friends together tomorrow?

1025
01:00:03,780 --> 01:00:05,216
- Yeah.
- Good.

1026
01:00:05,216 --> 01:00:07,656
Now, what should we play?

1027
01:00:07,656 --> 01:00:08,716
Superman?

1028
01:00:08,716 --> 01:00:10,340
Alright, arms out! Superman!

1029
01:00:10,340 --> 01:00:12,183
Stretch!

1030
01:00:12,183 --> 01:00:14,116
Wow!

1031
01:00:17,784 --> 01:00:20,208
They say the one who throws the punch
sleeps like a baby.

1032
01:00:20,208 --> 01:00:23,883
Even the punk who threatened the chief
seems pretty darn comfortable.

1033
01:00:25,848 --> 01:00:27,983
Hey, Lee Dong Jin, wake up.

1034
01:00:29,396 --> 01:00:31,216
Wake up, now!

1035
01:00:33,896 --> 01:00:36,507
God, because of you,
I made a total fool of myself

1036
01:00:36,507 --> 01:00:38,464
in front of the commissioner today...

1037
01:00:38,464 --> 01:00:41,616
God, why did I ever bring in
a blockhead like you?

1038
01:00:41,616 --> 01:00:43,240
You...

1039
01:00:43,240 --> 01:00:45,452
You have to risk your life.

1040
01:00:45,452 --> 01:00:47,649
Otherwise, we're both going down.

1041
01:00:47,649 --> 01:00:48,664
What?

1042
01:00:48,664 --> 01:00:50,140
What are you doing?

1043
01:00:50,140 --> 01:00:52,549
Move it and pack your stuff, you punk!

1044
01:00:59,749 --> 01:01:02,568
<i>♪ Every day on the bus to school ♪</i>

1045
01:01:02,568 --> 01:01:06,016
<i>♪ I like the girl
who always sits in the same seat ♪</i>

1046
01:01:06,016 --> 01:01:09,436
<i>♪ I sometimes deliberately stand beside her ♪</i>

1047
01:01:09,436 --> 01:01:12,816
<i>♪ But somehow I feel like
I'm not good enough ♪</i>

1048
01:01:12,816 --> 01:01:16,149
<i>♪ No, I'm fine. Don't worry about it ♪</i>

1049
01:01:16,149 --> 01:01:19,583
- <i>♪ I don't have a boyfriend now ♪</i>
- Come on out.

1050
01:01:19,583 --> 01:01:23,900
<i>♪ But why won't you say a word? ♪</i>

1051
01:01:23,900 --> 01:01:27,149
<i>♪ I know you really need me ♪</i>

1052
01:01:27,149 --> 01:01:31,749
<i>♪ You're too idealistic,
no woman is going to approach you ♪</i>

1053
01:01:31,749 --> 01:01:36,492
<i>♪ No woman is ever going
to make the first move ♪</i>

1054
01:01:36,492 --> 01:01:42,049
<i>♪ I'm no different, you know ♪</i>

1055
01:01:47,949 --> 01:01:50,883
<i>♪ Hesitating over something so simple ♪</i>

1056
01:01:50,883 --> 01:01:54,883
<i>♪ Watching you be so hopelessly
hesitant drives me crazy ♪</i>

1057
01:01:54,883 --> 01:01:58,949
<i>♪ You're too idealistic,
no woman is going to approach you ♪</i>

1058
01:01:58,949 --> 01:02:04,120
<i>♪ No woman is ever going
to make the first move ♪</i>

1059
01:02:04,120 --> 01:02:09,349
<i>♪ I'm no different, you know ♪</i>

1060
01:02:17,260 --> 01:02:20,316
I used to be better at this.

1061
01:02:22,649 --> 01:02:24,036
Yul's mom, sing one too.

1062
01:02:24,036 --> 01:02:25,649
- Oh, this is so much fun.
- Sing a song.

1063
01:02:25,649 --> 01:02:26,683
- Come on, sing.
- Me?

1064
01:02:26,683 --> 01:02:27,683
- No, I can't.
- We can't be the only ones singing.

1065
01:02:27,683 --> 01:02:28,683
- A song?
- Sing one!

1066
01:02:28,683 --> 01:02:32,949
- Sing a song!
- Sing a song!

1067
01:02:32,949 --> 01:02:37,783
[A Million Roses]

1068
01:02:41,948 --> 01:02:46,549
<i>♪ Long ago, from some distant star ♪</i>

1069
01:02:47,349 --> 01:02:53,216
<i>♪ When I came into this world ♪</i>

1070
01:02:53,216 --> 01:02:59,100
<i>♪ I heard a small voice ♪</i>

1071
01:02:59,100 --> 01:03:04,892
<i>♪ Telling me to come give love ♪</i>

1072
01:03:04,892 --> 01:03:08,292
<i>♪ That only blooms when you love ♪</i>

1073
01:03:08,292 --> 01:03:10,736
She's surprisingly romantic.

1074
01:03:10,736 --> 01:03:12,649
Exactly.

1075
01:03:12,649 --> 01:03:15,936
Why is she singing such a gloomy song?

1076
01:03:15,936 --> 01:03:18,549
She's killing the mood.

1077
01:03:18,549 --> 01:03:22,484
She's quite something.

1078
01:03:22,484 --> 01:03:28,272
<i>♪ Roses of love in bloom ♪</i>

1079
01:03:28,272 --> 01:03:33,988
<i>♪ Without a heart full of hate ♪</i>

1080
01:03:33,988 --> 01:03:39,948
<i>♪ When you give love without holding back ♪</i>

1081
01:03:39,948 --> 01:03:45,816
<i>♪ Millions and millions of roses bloom ♪</i>

1082
01:03:45,816 --> 01:03:51,728
<i>♪ And I can return to
our beautiful, beloved star ♪</i>

1083
01:03:51,728 --> 01:03:57,580
<i>♪ Without a heart full of hate ♪</i>

1084
01:03:57,580 --> 01:04:02,749
<i>♪ When you give love without holding back ♪</i>

1085
01:04:03,360 --> 01:04:09,224
<i>♪ Millions and millions of roses bloom ♪</i>

1086
01:04:09,224 --> 01:04:14,283
<i>♪ And I can return to
our beautiful, beloved star ♪</i>

1087
01:04:18,036 --> 01:04:21,120
<i>A special task force has been formed</i>

1088
01:04:21,120 --> 01:04:24,300
<i>to apprehend the serial killer
known as Kingfisher.</i>

1089
01:04:24,300 --> 01:04:26,705
<i>Accordingly, the scattered
investigative information and personnel</i>

1090
01:04:26,705 --> 01:04:28,792
<i>from each case
are expected to be consolidated,</i>

1091
01:04:28,792 --> 01:04:33,983
<i>with dedicated staff assigned
to accelerate the Kingfisher investigation.</i>

1092
01:05:04,983 --> 01:05:07,216
[Ok's Flower Shop]

1093
01:05:07,216 --> 01:05:14,116
[Ok's Flower Shop]

1094
01:05:23,016 --> 01:05:26,449
<i>Will this finally end with
Kingfisher's arrest?</i>

1095
01:05:26,449 --> 01:05:31,216
<i>Attention is now focused on
the newly formed Kingfisher task force.</i>

1096
01:06:34,160 --> 01:06:36,249
The mugging during the World Cup?

1097
01:06:36,249 --> 01:06:39,749
I believe it could provide a clue
to Kingfisher's identity.

1098
01:06:39,749 --> 01:06:41,620
Do you remember the caller's voice?

1099
01:06:41,620 --> 01:06:43,396
The message on the first card
they sent was...

1100
01:06:43,396 --> 01:06:45,840
"I hope you find your own beautiful scenery."

1101
01:06:45,840 --> 01:06:48,083
Can you tell me anything
about the person sending the flowers?

1102
01:06:48,083 --> 01:06:49,983
Who is it? The person you saw that day.

1103
01:06:49,983 --> 01:06:50,983
Some woman.

1104
01:06:50,983 --> 01:06:52,628
Why are you looking for that woman?

1105
01:06:52,628 --> 01:06:55,436
She either witnessed Kingfisher,
or she is Kingfisher.

1106
01:06:55,436 --> 01:06:57,549
You should still have
the voice message on your phone.

1107
01:06:57,549 --> 01:06:58,549
Who's taking this case?

1108
01:06:58,549 --> 01:07:02,160
We'll set a trap around Gu Jung Yeol
before Kingfisher makes a move.

1109
01:07:02,160 --> 01:07:03,783
Client meeting starts.

1110
01:07:03,783 --> 01:07:06,383
Let's go catch Kingfisher.

